9. A user visits a website but leaves within 10 seconds because they cannot find the navigation menu, which is hidden behind a small icon on a desktop screen. Analyze this design failure using the ”KISS” (Keep It Simple) principle.
ans: The KISS(keep It Simple) priniciple states that a design should be clearr and easy to understand especially for first time users. in this case, hiding the navigation menu behind a small icon on a desktop screen violates this priniciple.

Things that went wrong:
1. Overcomplication of Navigation
 •On desktop screens, users expect visible navigation menu (top or side).
 •Hiding it behind a small icon (hambuger menu )adds unnecessary complexity.
2. Poor visibility
•The navigation icon is small and not easily noticeable.
•According to KISS , important elements should be immediately visible , not hidden.
3. Mismatch with user expectations
•Hamburger menus are common on moblie devces not desktops.
•This breaks familiarity , incresing user confusion.
4. Increased Cognitive Load
•users must first figure out where the menu is before using the site.
•KISS emphasizes reducing thinking effort for users.

Solutions:
1. Display a clear , visible navigation bar on the desktop version.
2. Use simple labels like Home , About ,Services , Contact.
3. Reserve hidden for moblie screens only.
4. Make important actions obvious and accessible at first glance.

Conclusion
This design fails the KISS principle by hiding a critical feature(navigation) and making the interface unnecessarily complex. A simpler , more visible navigation would help users find inforamtion quickly and improves overall usability.

10. An e-commerce website has a URL structure like www.shop.com/prod?id=55&cat=9. Explain why this is bad for both users and Search Engines (SEO), and propose a better structure using Page Slugs
ans: The URL(www.shop.com/prod?id=55&cat=9) is a problematic URL.
Reasons this URL is bad:
1. For Users
•Not readable: Users cannot understand what the page is about.
•Not trustworthy: Random numbers and symbols look suspicious.
•Hard to remember or share:Users cannot guess or recall what the contents are.
2. For SEO
•No keywords:Search engines rely on words in URLS for rankong websites.
•Dynamic parameters are less SEO friendly.
•Lower click through rate:Users are less likely to click unclear URLS in search results.

Example of better URL:www.shop.com/electronics/smartphone-samsung-galaxy

Reasons for this URL being better:
1.Uses page slugs(human readable words).
2.Cleary shows category and product name.
3.Contains SEO keywords.
4.Easy to understand, remember and share.

Conclusion
The orginal URL strcture is bad because it is user infriendly and SEO unfriendly. Using clean URls with page slugs improve usablity , SEO ranking and click through rates making it ideal for an ecommerce website.